<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="089" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Assignment and override service (pin, exclude, change rule, removal preview); secure-child registration; K-2 pin test</title>
    <phase>3 Rules (WP3) — Procedure model (EB-D-148), wave W3-C</phase>
    <gate>081 merged; 080 schema live on dev (incl. sprk_createdbyperson on all four tables); owner OK for the live probes and -Apply runs; uac-r2 reviews every edit to its files</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Caller-checked writes on Secure records, a new secure child table and record-scoped rule sets joining the secure family, the shared ownership census and live role changes on dev: auth and tenant-isolation code.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security and tenant isolation across uac-r2- and ontology-owned files with binding review conditions from both.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P3-C</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits the uac-r2 files and census test listed below, which 081 and 086 also edit. Run /conflict-check before the PR.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>080, 081</deps>
    <tags>bff, api, auth, security, tenant-isolation, rules, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build the assignment and override service of notes/procedure-and-file-model.md section 6 (assign, pin, exclude a Procedure or rule, change a rule into the record's record-scoped set, remove an override behind 081's preview rules), caller-checked per 5.1. In the same change register sprk_procedureassignment and record-scoped rule sets (with their policies and versions) as secure children (5.2), rewrite the census waiver and guard, restore the NFR-05 depth list and add the K-2 pin test.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in IRecordOwnershipResolver, the uac-r2 secure child model, the ownership census and the Finance authorization filter.</role>

  <goal>Overrides are written only through this service after step 0 and the caller checks; rows are owned through the resolver; a Secure record's assignments and record rules live behind its wall; the census, lineage, role set, creator-person set and client child list agree.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Model 5.1 (rows; writes checked as the caller; census waiver; depth list; CIAM, K-1), 5.2 (census table, lineage edges, census guard controls, K-2, delete lists), 6.1-6.5 (sources, overrides, determinism, I-A1), 15 answer 2 (removal warning text and counting). The pre-EB-D-148 081 POML (git history: 081-ruleset-scope-service-ownership.poml) holds the secure-family mechanics that still apply (refusal probe 0x80040299, the #2084 shape; $SolutionHomes). Today: SecureChildLineage (Services/Access/SecureChildLineage.cs:175-178) files sprk_policy under sprk_matter and sprk_policyversion under sprk_policy; the census waives RuleSetService's policy creates (RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs:126, RuleSetServicePolicyWaiver); the access-conferring registry is MembershipOptions.AccessConferringRoles (Services/Ai/Membership/MembershipOptions.cs, seeded by MembershipOptionsDefaults) and sprk_organization is an identity table (:257). uac-r2's delete lists: core-record-delete-design.md on origin/work/unified-access-control-r2.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Procedures/ProcedureAssignmentService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/ProcedureAssignmentEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Access/SecureChildLineage.cs; Services/Dataverse/RecordOwnershipResolver.cs (OwnershipParentEntities only); Services/Dataverse/RecordCreatorPerson.cs; scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 + tests/scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.Tests.ps1; config/secure-record-owner-role.json; Infrastructure/Dataverse/SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion.cs; src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/utils/adapters/bffChildWriteAdapter.ts (all uac-r2)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs, RuleSetServiceNoMatterScopeGuardTests.cs, SecureFamilyConsistencyTests.cs, SecureChildNewCommandAgreementTests.cs (read), RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs; tests/unit/domain/Access/SecureChildLineageTests.cs; tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/SecureBuRoleDepthAssertionTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/Procedures/ProcedureAssignmentServiceTests.cs; tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/BillingLookupsConferNoAccessTests.cs (K-2)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs, EndpointMappingExtensions.cs (shared append points)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="model 5.1 (F1-c), 5.3">Every route in ProcedureAssignmentEndpoints.cs carries 099's step-0 flag. Then, as the caller: Write and AppendTo on the named core record through the Record path with FinanceDenial.UniformNotFound; Read on the Procedure (or on the rule's policy); the billing-admin privilege (BillingAdminAuthorization, fail closed). The core record id comes from the route; the type is fixed per route from the core-record list (InvoiceFamilyCoreRecordGuard's FilingCores), never from a free string.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 5.1">Rows are created as the application, owner from ResolveOwnerAsync(RecordOwnershipContext.ForParents(RecordOwnershipContext.ParentsOf(row), caller) with { RequestedBy = caller }), creator person = the caller. Record-scoped sprk_ruleset parent = its core record; its sprk_policy parent = the set; its sprk_policyversion parent = the policy. A resolver refusal writes nothing (RecordOwnerRefused).</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 6.2, 6.5 (I-A1)">Assignment modes: Follow latest (default), Pinned (a Procedure Version of that Procedure), Excluded. A second row for the same Procedure on the same record (same distance) → 409 assignment.duplicate. Rule-level rows follow the same rule.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 6.3">Exclude rule: row with rule, reason and an optional Firm. Change rule for this record: ONE BFF operation writing (1) an Exclude row for the base rule and (2) a record rule: a copy of the base rule's current parameters, edited, validated by PolicyVersionValidator and published immutable in the record's record-scoped set (created on first use; sprk_scope Record (100000002) for all firms, Firm record (100000003) with sprk_firm = F for one firm), storing "based on" = the base rule's policy version. A failure of either write undoes the other. A firm-named base rule can be changed only for its own firm (400). Record-rule codes use the new ontology D-13 key ontology-r1 gives.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 6.3 (remove), 15 answer 2">Remove an override: the row is deleted. For a changed-rule override the record rule is also switched Off (sprk_enabled No) and its open Signals close PolicyRetired through 081's shared selection method, behind a read-only preview: "Removing this override will close the rule it changed and remove pending decisions on active invoices." plus "N open invoices you can see are affected.", counted exactly as 081 counts (caller-readable only; no count on a rights fault); the result's count is caller-scoped. Other removals close nothing and re-check nothing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 5.2 (one change), F4-a">In this PR: lineage edges sprk_procedureassignment → core lookups, sprk_ruleset → core lookups, sprk_policy → sprk_ruleset (CitationLookups for the assignment: procedure, pinned version, excluded policy); OwnershipParentEntities gains both tables; OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES gains both; role JSON rows with live refusal-probe evidence; RecordCreatorPerson.StampedChildTables and the script ($SolutionHomes) for sprk_procedureassignment, sprk_ruleset, sprk_policy, sprk_policyversion; census entries. Procedure rule sets (sprk_procedure set, no record lookup) are NOT secure children.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 5.1, 5.2 (census guard, ontology O1, F3-e)">RuleSetServicePolicyWaiver is rewritten: every record-scoped sprk_ruleset writer and its sprk_policy / sprk_policyversion creates route through IRecordOwnershipResolver; the waiver remains only for Procedure rule sets. RuleSetServiceNoMatterScopeGuardTests is kept or narrowed so it still fails any sprk_matter write on a policy row.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 5.1 (depth list)">NFR-05: a SEPARATE non-throwing list beside SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion.GuardedPrivileges (unchanged) covers sprk_procedureassignment, sprk_ruleset, sprk_policy, sprk_policyversion and sprk_storedfile; an unresolved privilege name is a finding naming it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="model 5.2 K-2">sprk_billingfirm and sprk_billingresponsible are not in the access-conferring registry and no grant or share path reads them; ExternalModuleRegistry gains none of the new tables.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Not in this task: the resolver and its precedence (082); the 6.6 read models (084); the O-17 sweep that retires record-scoped sets whose record is gone (model 5.2, not assigned in the re-plan; raise it to the main session); delete code (uac-r2's planner and 080's cascade).</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md, ADR-010">Concrete service in AddFinanceModule; publish-size delta; no package; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 2026-10-21 (round 113 item 3; task 191)">Procedures are internal-only. Flagged-external systemusers on dev hold the same roles as internal users (Spaarke Basic User, Spaarke Console User, Spaarke Office Add In User) through their business unit's default team. So until uac-r2 task 191 lands, this task adds NO role privilege on sprk_procedure, sprk_procedureversion or sprk_procedureassignment without uac-r2's agreement; all access goes through the BFF.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 2026-10-23 (090 round 2)">090 already stamps sprk_createdbyperson on sprk_ruleset and sprk_procedureassignment (RecordCreatorPerson.StampedChildTables, the schema script's gate), so the creator column is trustworthy before this task's registration relies on it. The registration here is the first real create path for procedure assignments and record-scoped rule sets (today's sets are ClientDefault or Firm only) and is binding in full: SecureChildLineage, the RecordOwnershipResolver ownership parent (record-scoped set and assignment: the core record they name; Procedure-owned sets are not secure children), config/secure-record-owner-role.json with Read depth, the census entry, and a Restrict delete behaviour on the core-record lookups (uac Q10).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
