      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Owner routed with parents" location="RateCardImportService.ImportAsync (ResolveOwnerAsync with ForParents, Services/Finance/RateCardImportService.cs:200-211)">ForParents with RequestedBy; refusal writes nothing.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Role row with probe evidence" location="config/secure-record-owner-role.json (sprk_policy and sprk_policyversion entries)">Reason plus verbatim refusal.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Reconciler test fixture" location="tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Access/SecureChildReconcilerGateDecisionRecordTests.cs">Copy for version → policy → ruleset → core.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Merge origin/master; read notes/080 and 081; confirm sprk_createdbyperson exists on all four tables; read sprk_procedureassignment's and sprk_ruleset's OwnershipType live (must be UserOwned).</step>
    <step order="1">ProcedureAssignmentService and endpoints: assign, pin, exclude, exclude rule, change rule, remove with preview; authorization; ledger entry.</step>
    <step order="2">Secure child registration in one change; census rewrite and guards; NFR-05 list; K-2 test.</step>
    <step order="3">With the owner's OK: live refusal probes for both tables, Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1 -WhatIf / -Apply / -Verify, creator-person script dry run / -Apply / -Verify, live NFR-05 run. Notices to uac-r2 before and after.</step>
    <step order="4">dotnet build and test; Pester pin; client package test for OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES; publish-size delta; /conflict-check.</step>
    <step order="5">Reviews: uac-r2 (registration, authorization) and ontology-r1 (census guard, record-rule codes). Record both.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="7">Record deviations, probe evidence and -Apply / -Verify output in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/089-assignment-override-service.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any part of the secure-child registration cannot land in the same PR as the rest, STOP: a subset fails SecureFamilyConsistencyTests, SecureChildNewCommandAgreementTests or the census.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a refusal probe's create SUCCEEDS, delete the probe row, record it and STOP; ask uac-r2.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the live NFR-05 run reports a non-admin role whose Read on a listed table reaches the Secure business unit, STOP and raise 🔔 Human Input Required.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the owner has not given the OK for the probes and -Apply runs, do not run them; finish the code, do not open the PR, report.</trigger>
    <trigger>If "the billing privilege" of model 5.1 is meant to be another privilege than BillingAdminAuthorization's, or ontology-r1 has not given the record-rule code key, STOP and ask.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No service writes assignments or overrides (model 3.3 answers the table's overlap); RuleSetService writes rule sets without record scope.</existing>
    <extension>Registration extends existing lists. A new service because these writes are caller-checked against the record, which RuleSetService's admin routes are not; it reuses RuleSetService's validation and 081's close.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>No record can be pinned to a 2025 rate card, waive a rule or change one (O-4, O-10), and a record-specific rule on a Secure record would sit outside its wall (uac-r2 F1-a).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1, Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 (owner OK); Invoke-Pester</tool>
    <tool name="npm">the Spaarke.UI.Components test holding OWNERSHIP_CHILD_TABLES</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">live metadata reads; refusal probes (owner OK)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">ProcedureAssignmentService.cs, ProcedureAssignmentEndpoints.cs and the uac-r2 files above</output>
    <output type="test">ProcedureAssignmentServiceTests.cs, BillingLookupsConferNoAccessTests.cs and the ArchTests above</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/089-assignment-override-service.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Each route refuses a flagged-external caller, no systemuser row and a flag-read fault (negative); a caller without Write or AppendTo on the record gets the same 404 as for a non-existent record (byte-identical); without Read on the Procedure, or without the billing-admin privilege, the write is refused and nothing is written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Assign, pin, exclude and exclude-rule each write one row owned through the resolver with parents [the core record] and creator person = the caller; a Secure record's rows are owned by its Secure team; a second row for the same Procedure on the same record is 409 assignment.duplicate.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Change rule: one Exclude row plus one Published record rule in a record-scoped set with the right scope (Record, or Firm record with sprk_firm); the set's owner parents are [core record], the policy's [the set], the version's [the policy]; a second change reuses the set; a failure of the second write leaves neither; a firm-named base rule changed for another firm is refused 400; an invalid edited rule is refused by PolicyVersionValidator.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Remove: deleting a plain override closes no Signal; removing a changed-rule override switches the record rule Off and closes its open Signals through 081's shared method; the preview shows the removal warning with a caller-scoped count (3 affected, caller can Read 2 → "2 open invoices you can see are affected"), and a rights fault shows no count.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Census guard, must fire: a record-scoped rule-set create or a record-rule policy create that bypasses IRecordOwnershipResolver fails. Must not fire: a Procedure rule-set create and a Procedure-scoped policy create pass. Seeding proof recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SecureFamilyConsistencyTests, SecureChildNewCommandAgreementTests, the creator-person agreement test and Pester pin, SecureChildLineageTests and a reconciler test (version → policy → ruleset → core, secure and unsecure) pass; removing either table from any one list fails its test (seeding proof).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NFR-05: GuardedPrivileges and its pin are unchanged; the separate list covers the five tables; a missing privilege name gives exactly one finding naming it; the live run on dev is recorded with no finding.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">K-2: a test fails if the access-conferring registry holds any billing* column on a core table, and shows AccessConferringOnly resolution confers nothing through sprk_billingfirm or sprk_billingresponsible; ExternalModuleRegistry holds none of the new tables.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Notes record the probe refusals, -Apply / -Verify outputs, the owner's OK with dates and both reviews; publish-size delta; no package; no new HIGH CVE; /conflict-check run.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Two adversarial-review passes (auth, tenant isolation). Role rows and creator-person columns must be live on dev before 079 deploys the BFF; 079 re-runs both -Verify runs. 086 registers invoice Stored Files on the same files afterwards. spaarke-prototype 2026-10-21: answer questions h-j of notes/084-prototype-questions.md (removal-preview read, the typed parameter schema per rule type for change-rule, the request shapes of pin, exclude and change) in this task's notes, and send the path to spaarke-prototype. ontology-r1 080 review 2026-10-21: sprk_procedureversion.sprk_procedure is an alternate-key column and cannot be field-secured, so this task pins (test over the role privileges) that no non-BFF role holds Create or Write on sprk_procedureversion or sprk_procedureassignment. 080 PARENTAL LIMIT (2026-10-21, uac-r2 ACCEPT): Dataverse allows one parental (Delete = Cascade) relationship per table, so sprk_procedureassignment's three core lookups are RemoveLink and sprk_excludedpolicy is its only Cascade. The write validator's 'exactly one core lookup' rule applies to writes only. A stored row with zero core lookups is a sweep candidate, never a validation fault that makes it unreadable or stops a resolver run or the sweep.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
